==Post-match==
[[File:Mark_Schwarzer.jpg|thumb|Middlesbrough goalkeeper [[Mark Schwarzer]] was praised by his manager for recovering from an error.]]
Winning manager McClaren called the victory a "great reward" for Middlesbrough's players, managers and chairman [[Steve Gibson (businessman)|Steve Gibson]].<ref name=praises/> Captain [[Gareth Southgate]] also dedicated the win to the fans and Gibson, calling the chairman "the biggest fan we've got".<ref name=praises/> Gibson himself called the win "128 years in the making" and predicted the team would "kick on" from it.<ref name=praises/>

McClaren praised his goalkeeper Schwarzer for recovering from his error that allowed Bolton's goal, in order to make saves that won the match.<ref name=praises>{{cite news|title=McClaren praises Schwarzer|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/teams/m/middlesbrough/3489334.stm|access-date=1 April 2016|publisher=BBC Sport|date=29 February 2004}}</ref> He also said that the team should not become carried away by their qualification for Europe, and instead concentrate on the upcoming game against [[Birmingham City]].<ref name=praises/>

By winning the final, Middlesbrough qualified for [[2004–05 UEFA Cup|the following season's UEFA Cup]], their first European competition.<ref>{{cite news|title=Middlesbrough 3-0 Banik O|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/europe/3655976.stm|access-date=1 April 2016|publisher=BBC Sport|date=16 September 2004}}</ref> They beat [[Baník Ostrava]] in [[2004–05 UEFA Cup first round|the first round]] and [[2004–05 UEFA Cup group stage|came first in their group]] featuring [[Villarreal CF|Villarreal]], [[FK Partizan|Partizan]], [[SS Lazio|Lazio]] and [[Egaleo F.C.|Egaleo]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Boro 3-0 P Belgrade|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/europe/4087775.stm|access-date=1 April 2016|publisher=BBC Sport|date=15 December 2004}}</ref> They then defeated [[Grazer AK]] in the third round before being eliminated by [[Sporting CP|Sporting]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Sporting 1-0 M'brough (Agg: 4-2)|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/europe/4350037.stm|access-date=1 April 2016|publisher=BBC Sport|date=17 March 2005}}</ref>

Columnist Henry Winter ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]'' wrote that it was the best League Cup final since [[Luton Town F.C.|Luton Town]] beat Arsenal in [[1988 Football League Cup final|1988]].<ref name=winter>{{cite news|last1=Winter|first1=Henry|title=Middlesbrough's time to party|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/columnists/henrywinter/2374001/Middlesbroughs-time-to-party.html|access-date=1 April 2016|work=The Daily Telegraph|date=1 March 2004}}</ref> He praised all four of Middlesbrough's back line for their "alert defending", and noted the hard work in midfield by Boateng that allowed Zenden, Juninho and Mendieta to create chances.<ref name=winter/> He also lauded Bolton's fans and the efforts of Okocha, Djorkaeff and Davies, while noting how Bolton's Campo was effective despite "the odd pantomime [[Simulation (Association football)|dive]]".<ref name=winter/> Alan Smith of the same newspaper opined that 33-year-old Southgate was the most deserving winner, as reward for his consistency since arriving in an "average" Boro side in 2001. Southgate's only other medal had come in the same competition for Aston Villa [[1996 Football League Cup final|eight years prior]].<ref>{{cite news|last1=Smith|first1=Alan|title=Southgate gets due reward for years of dedication|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/columnists/alansmith/2374023/Southgate-gets-due-reward-for-years-of-dedication.html|access-date=1 April 2016|work=The Daily Telegraph|date=1 March 2004}}</ref>

In June 2013, Juninho said that winning the League Cup with Middlesbrough was better than when he won the [[FIFA World Cup]] with [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] in [[2002 FIFA World Cup|2002]].<ref>{{cite news|last1=Oliver-Gaz|first1=George|title=Five reasons why the League Cup is better than the World Cup|url=http://www.gazettelive.co.uk/sport/football/five-reasons-league-cup-beats-4799766|access-date=1 April 2016|work=Gazette Live|date=1 July 2013}}</ref>

